  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Determining the Existence of a Limit for a Fractional Function</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[</p>Determine whether the limit of the function below exist or not.</p>


<br> \(\displaystyle \lim_{(x,y) \longrightarrow ({@value_of_x@}, {@value_of_y@})} \frac{@expr_numerator@}{@expr_denominator@} \). If the limit doesn't exist click NO as your answer.


<br>
<button id="btn1yes" type="button" style="font-size:16px" onclick="reveal('1');">Yes</button>
 <button id="btn1no" type="button" style="font-size:16px" onclick="hide('1');">No</button> [[feedback:prtyn1]]
<div id="input1" style="display:none;">[[input:ans_yn1]] [[validation:ans_yn1]]</div>
<br>
<div id="example1" style="display:none;">
    For:  \(  \displaystyle \lim_{(x,y) \longrightarrow ({@value_of_x@}, {@value_of_y@})} \left({@expr_numerator@} \right) = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] and \( \displaystyle \lim_{(x,y) \longrightarrow ({@value_of_x@}, {@value_of_y@})} \left({@expr_denominator@}\right) = \)[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]].
    <br> From this we can conclude \( \displaystyle \lim_{(x,y) \longrightarrow ({@value_of_x@}, {@value_of_y@})} h(x, y)= \)  [[input:ans3]]  [[validation:ans3]]
<br> [[feedback:prt1]]
</div>



