    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked solution</h3>

<br>Let \( \displaystyle h(x,y)= \frac{@expr_numerator@}{@expr_denominator@} \)
<p>To find the limit of the given expression as \(x\) approaches {@value_of_x@} and \(y\) approaches {@value_of_y@}, we can simply substitute these values in the expression and simplify:</p>
<p> For:  \( \displaystyle \lim_{(x,y) \longrightarrow ({@value_of_x@}, {@value_of_y@})} \left({@expr_numerator@} \right) ={@ta_1@} \)  and \( \displaystyle \lim_{(x,y) \longrightarrow ({@value_of_x@}, {@value_of_y@})} \left({@expr_denominator@}\right) ={@ta_2@} \).</p>
<br> From this we can conclude \(  \displaystyle \lim_{(x,y) \longrightarrow ({@value_of_x@}, {@value_of_y@})} h(x, y)=\lim_{(x,y) \longrightarrow ({@value_of_x@}, {@value_of_y@})}  \frac{@expr_numerator@}{@expr_denominator@}={@ta_3@} \).]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber/>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2023060500</text>
    </stackversion>
    <questionvariables>
      <text>/*the limit will always  exist for this function*/
a1:rand(10)+1;
bb:rand(6)+1;
cc:rand(8)+1;
dd:rand(9);
expr_numerator: a1*x^2*y+bb*x*y;
expr_denominator: cc*x^2+dd;

value_of_x: rand_with_prohib(-5,5,[0]);
value_of_y: rand_with_step(-5,5,1);
ta_1: at(expr_numerator, [x=value_of_x, y=value_of_y]);
ta_2: at(expr_denominator, [x=value_of_x, y=value_of_y]);
ta_3: ta_1/ta_2;


ta_yn1: true ;</text>
    </questionvariables>
